On Sun, Oct 12, 2014 at 5:38 AM, Gleki Arxokuna <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>
wrote:


> klaji doesnt have "from" place.
>

Nor a "to" place, in the sense that I think you mean. klaji3 is for
buildings and such located on the side of klaji1, such that they can be
accessed from it. The idea being that the end points of streets are not
particularly interesting or relevant.

 lo ckule .e lo muzga .e lo malsi cu te klaji fi la bi moi
 The school and the museum and the church are on 8th Street.


> how would you express them when they are absent?
>

"fe'e co'a", "fe'e co'u"?


> How to describe two-way doors, bridges and streets?
>

"relselfa'a" (vs. "pavyselfa'a")?

mu'o mi'e xorxes

